2. **Color Patterns and Markings**: The coloration of the American alligator can vary depending on its age and habitat. Juveniles often have a more vibrant pattern of dark green or olive with lighter spots and stripes, while adults tend to have a darker, more uniform coloration ranging from olive-green to brownish-black. The skin texture appears rough and scaly, with a noticeable ridge running along the back.

